oom_request.md 01_planning_rules.md 02_sessions.csv 03_room_options.csv 04_initial_facility_note_2026-06-01.md output_contract.md staged_update/05_facility_update_2026-06-10.md; do echo '###' $f; echo '---'; cat \"$f\"; echo; done", "timeout_seconds": 120}, "result": "### 00_room_request.md\n---\n# Room Request\n\nRequest date: 2026-06-03\n\nBayview Civic Center needs a room assignment packet for three community workshops on 2026-06-18.\n\nThe packet should assign one room to each session in `02_sessions.csv`, keep total room cost at or below `$800`, and make any later coordinator update easy to apply without discarding correct completed work.\n\nIf a newer facility update conflicts with an older room note, use the newer dated facility update for room availability.\n\n### 01_planning_rules.md\n---\n# Planning Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-06-03\n\n## Source Reliability\n\n- Use the newest dated facility source for room availability when facility notes conflict.\n- Session requirements in `02_sessions.csv` control capacity, time block, equipment, and room-trait needs.\n- Room traits and base costs come from `03_room_options.csv` unless a newer facility update changes room availability.\n\n## Hard Requirements\n\n- Assign every session to exactly one room.\n- Use rooms that are available for the session time block.\n- Room capacity must be at least the session attendee count.\n- If a session needs a projector, demo table, quiet room, or loading access, the assigned room must provide it.\n- Total room cost must be at or below `$800`.\n- Prefer the lowest-cost valid room for each session unless preserving a correct existing assignment after an update is more important.\n\n## Replanning Rule\n\nIf a coordinator update makes part of the initial plan invalid, repair only the affected part when possible. Preserve correct assignments that still satisfy all requirements.\n\n### 02_sessions.csv\n---\nsession_id,session,attendees,time_block,needs_projector,needs_demo_table,needs_quiet_room,needs_loading_access\nS-101,Safety Orientation,22,morning,yes,no,no,no\nS-102,Inventory Lab,16,afternoon,yes,yes,no,yes\nS-103,Benefits Clinic,12,morning,no,no,yes,no\n\n### 03_room_options.csv\n---\nroom,capacity,available_time_blocks,projector,demo_table,quiet_room,loading_access,cost\nHarbor Hall,30,morning;afternoon,yes,no,no,no,300\nBay Workshop,18,afternoon,yes,yes,no,yes,250\nCedar Room,16,morning;afternoon,no,no,yes,no,150\nDelta Annex,20,afternoon,yes,yes,no,yes,320\nElm Room,14,morning;afternoon,no,no,yes,no,125\n\n### 04_initial_facility_note_2026-06-01.md\n---\n# Initial Facility Note\n\nDate: 2026-06-01\n\nAll rooms listed in `03_room_options.csv` are available for booking on 2026-06-18.\n\nBay Workshop is the lowest-cost room with a demo table, projector, and loading access for an afternoon lab.\n\nDelta Annex is also available for the afternoon, but it costs more than Bay Workshop and should be treated as a backup unless another source changes availability.\n\n### output_contract.md\n---\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/initial_room_plan.md`\n\nRecord the room assignment plan before any coordinator update is introduced.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every session in `02_sessions.csv`.\n- The selected room for each session.\n- The room evidence that supports each assignment: capacity, time block, required equipment or room trait, and cost.\n- The initial total room cost and budget status against the `$800` ceiling.\n- Any backup room considered for a fragile assignment.\n\n## `answer/update_response.md`\n\nAfter the coordinator update is introduced, explain what changed and how the plan should be repaired.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The update source and date.\n- The specific room assignment affected by the update.\n- Which original assignments remain valid and should be preserved.\n- The replacement assignment and why it satisfies the same session requirements.\n- The revised cost effect.\n\n## `answer/final_room_plan.md`\n\nWrite the final room assignment package after applying the update.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One final room assignment for every session.\n- The final total room cost and remaining budget.\n- A short note confirming the same workshop objective is still covered.\n- A short note naming preserved work from the initial plan.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not relax hard room requirements unless a local file explicitly says to.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n\n### staged_update/05_facility_update_2026-06-10.md\n---\n# Facility Update\n\nDate: 2026-06-10\n\nBay Workshop is closed for floor repair on 2026-06-18 and cannot host the Inventory Lab.\n\nDelta Annex has been released for general booking on 2026-06-18 afternoon. It has projector, demo table, and loading access available for the Inventory Lab.\n\nHarbor Hall and Elm Room availability is unchanged.\n\nThe workshop objective has not changed: cover all three sessions with valid rooms and stay within the `$800` ceiling."}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "ls -la answer && find answer -maxdepth 2 -type f -print -exec sh -c 'echo ---; cat \"$1\"' _ {} \\;", "timeout_seconds": 120}, "result": "total 0\ndrwxr-xr-x@  2 douglas  staff   64 Jun 15 19:24 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 11 douglas  staff  352 Jun 15 19:24 .."}], "usage": {"requests": 3, "tool_calls": 4, "input_tokens": 3270, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "input_audio_tokens": 0, "cache_audio_read_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 597, "output_audio_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 3867, "details": {}}, "cost": {"usd": null, "estimated": false}, "mod